    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), across the three places the tier was wired in:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipTier` string enum (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) from the `Owner` schema and replaced it with `membershipLevel`: an `int32` with `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, documenting that it starts at 1, +1 for a present email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3, with level 4 reserved for tenure. This regenerates `OwnerDto` (the DTO isn't checked in \u2014 it's generated by the openapi-generator plugin), so the old `MembershipTierEnum` and `getMembershipTier()` are gone and a `getMembershipLevel()` appears.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the tier expression with `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))`, dropping the old household-size/GOLD logic.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier. I map the DTO before logging so the audit uses the single computed value: `Owner created: id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`.\n\nThe full suite (34 tests, including the level/tier checks in Cp15/Cp21/Cp23/Cp24) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
